inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>JIN DONGZHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUZAKI KAZUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA KENGO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAWAKI KOSUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ABE, FUMIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASEGAWA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JIN, DONGZHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUZAKI, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, KENGO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAWAKI, KOSUKE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A rotary sensor (10) provided with a first rotor (11) fixed on a shaft in a specified position in the axial direction, a second rotor (12) fixed on the shaft (5) in a position next to the first rotor, and a magnetic core (13) arranged around the first rotor and having a resonance coil (13c) that constitutes a magnetic circuit in conjunction with the first rotor. The first rotor (11), which is composed of a magnetic member made of an insulator, forms a nonuniform magnetic field between it and the magnetic core. The second rotor (12) has a conductive part that transverses the nonuniform magnetic field of different strength that depends on the relative rotation angle difference between the shaft position where the first rotor is fixed and the shaft position where the second rotor is fixed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention a trait à un détecteur rotatif (10) pourvu d'un premier rotor (11) fixé sur un arbre dans une position déterminée dans le sens axial ainsi que d'un second rotor (12) fixé sur l'arbre (5) à proximité du premier et d'un noyau magnétique (13), placé autour du premier rotor et possédant une bobine de résonance (13c) constituant un circuit magnétique de concert avec le premier rotor. Le premier rotor (11), qui comprend un élément magnétique fait d'un isolant, produit un champ magnétique non uniforme s'étendant entre lui et le noyau magnétique. Le second rotor (12) est pourvu d'une partie conductrice transverse au champ magnétique non uniforme, d'une intensité différente, tributaire de la différence d'angle de rotation relative entre la position de l'arbre sur lequel est fixé le premier rotor et la position de l'arbre sur lequel est fixé le second rotor.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>